            <ArticleTitle>Cystic degeneration of the patella after arthroscopic chondroplasty and subchondral bone perforation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>366-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chondromalacia of the patella is frequently encountered in patients with anterior knee pain. Arthroscopic chondroplasty with perforation of subchondral bone remains a popular treatment alternative in spite of the inferior mechanical properties of the fibrocartilaginous tissue that this procedure is designed to promote. We report a case of cystic degeneration of the patella as a previously unrecognized complication following the procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
